research/audit/wave7-dispatch/certifier-lem-minimal-cauchy-filter-associated-to-a-cauchy-filter.log-6274-research/audit/wave7-topology-uniform.provenance.jsonl-14-{"id":"thm-entourage-uniformities-are-generated-by-gauges","statement":"ai-altered","proof":"ai-altered","evidence":"established-knowledge","urls":["https://math.berkeley.edu/~wodzicki/H104.F13/UniformStructure-alt.pdf","https://www.mat.univie.ac.at/~mike/teaching/ss16/general_topology.pdf"],"rationale":"ESCALATED TO ALPHA. The sources prove every uniformity is generated by pseudometrics but assume an ordinary classical background; the item isolates DC as sufficient. The theorem is standard, but no source with the same foundational hypothesis surfaced. ALPHA CONCURRENCE: Representation of an arbitrary uniformity by a family of pseudometrics is a standard uniform-space theorem, and the current proof follows the usual normal-sequence construction. Stating DC as sufficient is an explicit choice calibration, so the local form is established and ai-altered.","alpha_concurred":true,"at":"2026-08-08"}
research/audit/wave7-dispatch/certifier-lem-minimal-cauchy-filter-associated-to-a-cauchy-filter.log:6275:research/audit/wave7-topology-uniform.provenance.jsonl-15-{"id":"thm-three-definitions-of-uniform-space-are-equivalent","statement":"ai-altered","proof":"ai-generated","evidence":"established-knowledge","urls":["https://encyclopediaofmath.org/wiki/Uniform_space","https://math.berkeley.edu/~wodzicki/H104.F13/UniformStructure-alt.pdf","https://www.mat.univie.ac.at/~mike/teaching/ss16/general_topology.pdf"],"rationale":"ESCALATED TO ALPHA. Literature gives the entourage-cover equivalence and pseudometric generation, but not this exact compound ZF/DC calibration. This is a standard synthesis, not an invented theorem; the proof composes the preceding results. ALPHA CONCURRENCE: Entourage, uniform-cover, and gauge formulations are the standard equivalent presentations of uniform spaces. The nonempty-carrier repair and split ZF/DC bookkeeping adapt the classical package to this library's proper-filter convention without creating new mathematics.","alpha_concurred":true,"at":"2026-08-08"}
research/audit/wave7-dispatch/certifier-lem-minimal-cauchy-filter-associated-to-a-cauchy-filter.log-6276-research/audit/wave7-topology-uniform.provenance.jsonl-16-{"id":"def-cauchy-filter-in-a-uniform-space","statement":"literature-derived","proof":"not-applicable","evidence":"exact-source","urls":["https://math.berkeley.edu/~wodzicki/H104.F13/UniformStructure-alt.pdf","https://encyclopediaofmath.org/wiki/Uniform_space"],"rationale":"The sources use the same requirement that for every entourage a filter member have square contained in it; notation and equivalent cover wording are the only differences.","alpha_concurred":false,"at":"2026-08-08"}
research/audit/wave7-dispatch/certifier-lem-minimal-cauchy-filter-associated-to-a-cauchy-filter.log-6277-research/audit/wave7-topology-uniform.provenance.jsonl-17-{"id":"lem-convergent-filters-are-cauchy","statement":"literature-derived","proof":"ai-altered","evidence":"exact-source","urls":["https://math.berkeley.edu/~wodzicki/H104.F13/UniformStructure-alt.pdf"],"rationale":"Wodzicki Exercise 41 states exactly that every filter convergent in the uniform topology is Cauchy. The item supplies the standard symmetric-root proof, with a missing direct citation proposed at A3.","alpha_concurred":false,"at":"2026-08-08"}
research/audit/wave7-dispatch/certifier-lem-minimal-cauchy-filter-associated-to-a-cauchy-filter.log-6278-research/audit/wave7-topology-uniform.provenance.jsonl-18-{"id":"lem-cauchy-filter-with-a-cluster-point-converges","statement":"literature-derived","proof":"ai-altered","evidence":"exact-source","urls":["https://math.berkeley.edu/~wodzicki/H104.F13/UniformStructure-alt.pdf"],"rationale":"Wodzicki Exercise 45 states that every adherence point of a Cauchy filter is its convergence point. The proof expands this and needs the induced-topology citation recorded at A3.","alpha_concurred":false,"at":"2026-08-08"}
