research/audit/wave7-dispatch/certifier-thm-complete-and-totally-bounded-uniform-spaces-are-compact.log-10191-research/audit/wave7-dispatch/audit-beta-topology-uniform-a4-recovery.log:5027:{"id":"thm-complete-and-totally-bounded-uniform-spaces-are-compact","statement":"ai-altered","proof":"ai-generated","evidence":"established-knowledge","urls":["https://encyclopediaofmath.org/wiki/Uniform_space"],"rationale":"ESCALATED TO ALPHA. Complete-plus-precompact implies compact is standard, but the item explicitly assumes only the ultrafilter lemma, whereas the source works classically. The local proof verifies that weaker assumption; its extra full-Choice citation is an A3 defect. ALPHA CONCURRENCE: Complete plus totally bounded implies compact is a classical uniform-space theorem. The proof through convergence of ultrafilters uses precisely the ultrafilter lemma; making that weak-choice hypothesis explicit is a standard foundational calibration, not invention.","alpha_concurred":true,"at":"2026-08-08"}
