research/audit/wave7-dispatch/audit-beta-topology-uniform.log-56811-['def-uniform-cover-space','ai-altered','semantic-source',[E,W],'not-applicable','Encyclopedia of Mathematics gives the uniform-cover axioms and Wodzicki develops the associated cover relation. The item uses an equivalent star-refinement presentation and currently overstates equivalence on the empty carrier under the library proper-filter convention.'],
research/audit/wave7-dispatch/audit-beta-topology-uniform.log-56812-['lem-entourage-and-uniform-cover-dictionary','ai-altered','semantic-source',[E,W],'ai-altered','The sources give the standard equivalence between entourage and uniform-cover formulations. The item spells out both constructions; its cover-to-entourage direction needs the nonempty-carrier qualification recorded for A3.'],
research/audit/wave7-dispatch/audit-beta-topology-uniform.log-56813-['def-gauge-of-pseudometrics','ai-altered','semantic-source',[E,V,B],'not-applicable','The sources define a uniformity from finite intersections of pseudometric balls. The item calls the family a gauge and bundles topology and uniform-continuity clauses; under the local proper-filter convention it also needs a nonempty carrier.'],
research/audit/wave7-dispatch/audit-beta-topology-uniform.log-56814-['lem-normal-sequences-of-entourages','ai-altered','established-knowledge',[W,V],'ai-generated','ESCALATED TO ALPHA. Iterated symmetric entourage roots are the standard normal-sequence construction in both sources, but the published Statement makes the strictly weaker foundational hypothesis DC explicit and no located source states that same choice-calibrated proposition. It is established construction, not novel; the recursion proof is local.'],
research/audit/wave7-dispatch/audit-beta-topology-uniform.log-56815-['lem-pseudometric-from-a-normal-entourage-sequence','literature-derived','exact-source',[W,V],'ai-altered','Both sources state the normal-sequence metrization lemma with the same dyadic control inclusions and path-infimum pseudometric construction. The proof is a notation-adjusted expansion of that argument.'],
research/audit/wave7-dispatch/audit-beta-topology-uniform.log-56816-['thm-entourage-uniformities-are-generated-by-gauges','ai-altered','established-knowledge',[W,V],'ai-altered','ESCALATED TO ALPHA. The sources prove every uniformity is generated by pseudometrics, but assume an ordinary classical background; the item isolates DC as sufficient. The mathematical theorem is standard, but no source with the same foundational hypothesis surfaced.'],
research/audit/wave7-dispatch/audit-beta-topology-uniform.log:56817:['thm-three-definitions-of-uniform-space-are-equivalent','ai-altered','established-knowledge',[E,W,V],'ai-generated','ESCALATED TO ALPHA. Literature gives the entourage-cover equivalence and pseudometric generation, but not this exact compound ZF/DC calibration. This is a standard synthesis, not an invented theorem; the local proof composes the preceding dictionary and gauge results.'],
research/audit/wave7-dispatch/audit-beta-topology-uniform.log-56818-['def-cauchy-filter-in-a-uniform-space','literature-derived','exact-source',[W,E],'not-applicable','The sources use the same requirement that for every entourage a filter member have square contained in it; notation and the equivalent uniform-cover wording are the only differences.'],
research/audit/wave7-dispatch/audit-beta-topology-uniform.log-56819-['lem-convergent-filters-are-cauchy','literature-derived','exact-source',[W],'ai-altered','Wodzicki Exercise 41 states exactly that every filter convergent in the uniform topology is Cauchy. The item supplies the standard symmetric-root proof, with a missing direct citation proposed at A3.'],
research/audit/wave7-dispatch/audit-beta-topology-uniform.log-56820-['lem-cauchy-filter-with-a-cluster-point-converges','literature-derived','exact-source',[W],'ai-altered','Wodzicki Exercise 45 states that every adherence point of a Cauchy filter is its convergence point. The local proof expands this and needs the induced-topology citation recorded at A3.'],
research/audit/wave7-dispatch/audit-beta-topology-uniform.log-56821-['def-complete-uniform-space','literature-derived','exact-source',[W,C],'not-applicable','Both sources define a complete uniform space as one in which every Cauchy filter converges, exactly as the item does.'],
research/audit/wave7-dispatch/audit-beta-topology-uniform.log-56822-['def-uniform-embedding-and-uniform-isomorphism','ai-altered','semantic-source',[E,W],'not-applicable','The literature uses the same uniform-isomorphism and subspace-uniformity notions. The item packages the embedding and isomorphism definitions in library notation.'],
research/audit/wave7-dispatch/audit-beta-topology-uniform.log-56823-['def-completion-of-a-uniform-space','ai-altered','semantic-source',[E,W,C],'not-applicable','The sources define completion by a complete separated target with dense canonical image and induced original uniformity. The item explicitly permits a noninjective Hausdorff reflection map, an equivalent convention for nonseparated inputs.'],
