research/audit/wave7-dispatch/audit-beta-topology-uniform.log:205288:+{"id":"thm-three-definitions-of-uniform-space-are-equivalent","statement":"ai-altered","proof":"ai-generated","evidence":"established-knowledge","urls":["https://encyclopediaofmath.org/wiki/Uniform_space","https://math.berkeley.edu/~wodzicki/H104.F13/UniformStructure-alt.pdf","https://www.mat.univie.ac.at/~mike/teaching/ss16/general_topology.pdf"],"rationale":"ESCALATED TO ALPHA. Literature gives the entourage-cover equivalence and pseudometric generation, but not this exact compound ZF/DC calibration. This is a standard synthesis, not an invented theorem; the proof composes the preceding results.","alpha_concurred":false,"at":"2026-08-08"}
research/audit/wave7-dispatch/audit-beta-topology-uniform.log-205289-+{"id":"def-cauchy-filter-in-a-uniform-space","statement":"literature-derived","proof":"not-applicable","evidence":"exact-source","urls":["https://math.berkeley.edu/~wodzicki/H104.F13/UniformStructure-alt.pdf","https://encyclopediaofmath.org/wiki/Uniform_space"],"rationale":"The sources use the same requirement that for every entourage a filter member have square contained in it; notation and equivalent cover wording are the only differences.","alpha_concurred":false,"at":"2026-08-08"}
research/audit/wave7-dispatch/audit-beta-topology-uniform.log-205290-+{"id":"lem-convergent-filters-are-cauchy","statement":"literature-derived","proof":"ai-altered","evidence":"exact-source","urls":["https://math.berkeley.edu/~wodzicki/H104.F13/UniformStructure-alt.pdf"],"rationale":"Wodzicki Exercise 41 states exactly that every filter convergent in the uniform topology is Cauchy. The item supplies the standard symmetric-root proof, with a missing direct citation proposed at A3.","alpha_concurred":false,"at":"2026-08-08"}
research/audit/wave7-dispatch/audit-beta-topology-uniform.log-205291-+{"id":"lem-cauchy-filter-with-a-cluster-point-converges","statement":"literature-derived","proof":"ai-altered","evidence":"exact-source","urls":["https://math.berkeley.edu/~wodzicki/H104.F13/UniformStructure-alt.pdf"],"rationale":"Wodzicki Exercise 45 states that every adherence point of a Cauchy filter is its convergence point. The proof expands this and needs the induced-topology citation recorded at A3.","alpha_concurred":false,"at":"2026-08-08"}
research/audit/wave7-dispatch/audit-beta-topology-uniform.log-205292-+{"id":"def-complete-uniform-space","statement":"literature-derived","proof":"not-applicable","evidence":"exact-source","urls":["https://math.berkeley.edu/~wodzicki/H104.F13/UniformStructure-alt.pdf","https://encyclopediaofmath.org/wiki/Complete_uniform_space"],"rationale":"Both sources define completeness as convergence of every Cauchy filter, exactly as the item does.","alpha_concurred":false,"at":"2026-08-08"}
research/audit/wave7-dispatch/audit-beta-topology-uniform.log-205293-+{"id":"def-uniform-embedding-and-uniform-isomorphism","statement":"ai-altered","proof":"not-applicable","evidence":"semantic-source","urls":["https://encyclopediaofmath.org/wiki/Uniform_space","https://math.berkeley.edu/~wodzicki/H104.F13/UniformStructure-alt.pdf"],"rationale":"The literature uses the same uniform-isomorphism and subspace-uniformity notions. The item packages the embedding and isomorphism definitions in library notation.","alpha_concurred":false,"at":"2026-08-08"}
research/audit/wave7-dispatch/audit-beta-topology-uniform.log-205294-+{"id":"def-completion-of-a-uniform-space","statement":"ai-altered","proof":"not-applicable","evidence":"semantic-source","urls":["https://encyclopediaofmath.org/wiki/Uniform_space","https://math.berkeley.edu/~wodzicki/H104.F13/UniformStructure-alt.pdf","https://encyclopediaofmath.org/wiki/Complete_uniform_space"],"rationale":"The sources define completion by a complete separated target with dense canonical image and induced original uniformity. The item explicitly permits a noninjective Hausdorff reflection map, the equivalent convention for nonseparated inputs.","alpha_concurred":false,"at":"2026-08-08"}
