research/audit/wave7-dispatch/audit-beta-topology-uniform.log-222953-+{"id":"def-uniform-cover-space","statement":"ai-altered","proof":"not-applicable","evidence":"semantic-source","urls":["https://encyclopediaofmath.org/wiki/Uniform_space","https://math.berkeley.edu/~wodzicki/H104.F13/UniformStructure-alt.pdf"],"rationale":"Encyclopedia of Mathematics gives the uniform-cover axioms and Wodzicki develops the associated cover relation. The item uses an equivalent star-refinement presentation and currently overstates equivalence on the empty carrier under the library proper-filter convention.","alpha_concurred":false,"at":"2026-08-08"}
research/audit/wave7-dispatch/audit-beta-topology-uniform.log-222954-+{"id":"lem-entourage-and-uniform-cover-dictionary","statement":"ai-altered","proof":"ai-altered","evidence":"semantic-source","urls":["https://encyclopediaofmath.org/wiki/Uniform_space","https://math.berkeley.edu/~wodzicki/H104.F13/UniformStructure-alt.pdf"],"rationale":"The sources give the standard equivalence between entourage and uniform-cover formulations. The item spells out both constructions; its cover-to-entourage direction needs the nonempty-carrier qualification recorded for A3.","alpha_concurred":false,"at":"2026-08-08"}
research/audit/wave7-dispatch/audit-beta-topology-uniform.log-222955-+{"id":"def-gauge-of-pseudometrics","statement":"ai-altered","proof":"not-applicable","evidence":"semantic-source","urls":["https://encyclopediaofmath.org/wiki/Uniform_space","https://www.mat.univie.ac.at/~mike/teaching/ss16/general_topology.pdf","https://u.math.biu.ac.il/~megereli/TGrNotes070217.pdf"],"rationale":"The sources define a uniformity from finite intersections of pseudometric balls. The item calls the family a gauge and bundles topology and uniform-continuity clauses; under the local proper-filter convention it also needs a nonempty carrier.","alpha_concurred":false,"at":"2026-08-08"}
research/audit/wave7-dispatch/audit-beta-topology-uniform.log-222956-+{"id":"lem-normal-sequences-of-entourages","statement":"ai-altered","proof":"ai-generated","evidence":"established-knowledge","urls":["https://math.berkeley.edu/~wodzicki/H104.F13/UniformStructure-alt.pdf","https://www.mat.univie.ac.at/~mike/teaching/ss16/general_topology.pdf"],"rationale":"ESCALATED TO ALPHA. Iterated symmetric entourage roots are the standard normal-sequence construction in both sources, but the Statement makes the strictly weaker foundational hypothesis DC explicit and no located source states that same choice-calibrated proposition. It is established, not novel; the recursion proof is local.","alpha_concurred":false,"at":"2026-08-08"}
research/audit/wave7-dispatch/audit-beta-topology-uniform.log-222957-+{"id":"lem-pseudometric-from-a-normal-entourage-sequence","statement":"literature-derived","proof":"ai-altered","evidence":"exact-source","urls":["https://math.berkeley.edu/~wodzicki/H104.F13/UniformStructure-alt.pdf","https://www.mat.univie.ac.at/~mike/teaching/ss16/general_topology.pdf"],"rationale":"Both sources state the normal-sequence metrization lemma with the same dyadic control inclusions and path-infimum pseudometric construction. The proof is a notation-adjusted expansion.","alpha_concurred":false,"at":"2026-08-08"}
research/audit/wave7-dispatch/audit-beta-topology-uniform.log-222958-+{"id":"thm-entourage-uniformities-are-generated-by-gauges","statement":"ai-altered","proof":"ai-altered","evidence":"established-knowledge","urls":["https://math.berkeley.edu/~wodzicki/H104.F13/UniformStructure-alt.pdf","https://www.mat.univie.ac.at/~mike/teaching/ss16/general_topology.pdf"],"rationale":"ESCALATED TO ALPHA. The sources prove every uniformity is generated by pseudometrics but assume an ordinary classical background; the item isolates DC as sufficient. The theorem is standard, but no source with the same foundational hypothesis surfaced.","alpha_concurred":false,"at":"2026-08-08"}
