research/audit/wave7-dispatch/audit-beta-topology-uniform.log-307129-+{"id":"lem-entourage-and-uniform-cover-dictionary","statement":"ai-altered","proof":"ai-altered","evidence":"semantic-source","urls":["https://encyclopediaofmath.org/wiki/Uniform_space","https://math.berkeley.edu/~wodzicki/H104.F13/UniformStructure-alt.pdf"],"rationale":"The sources give the standard equivalence between entourage and uniform-cover formulations. The item spells out both constructions; its cover-to-entourage direction needs the nonempty-carrier qualification recorded for A3.","alpha_concurred":false,"at":"2026-08-08"}
research/audit/wave7-dispatch/audit-beta-topology-uniform.log-307130-+{"id":"def-gauge-of-pseudometrics","statement":"ai-altered","proof":"not-applicable","evidence":"semantic-source","urls":["https://encyclopediaofmath.org/wiki/Uniform_space","https://www.mat.univie.ac.at/~mike/teaching/ss16/general_topology.pdf","https://u.math.biu.ac.il/~megereli/TGrNotes070217.pdf"],"rationale":"The sources define a uniformity from finite intersections of pseudometric balls. The item calls the family a gauge and bundles topology and uniform-continuity clauses; under the local proper-filter convention it also needs a nonempty carrier.","alpha_concurred":false,"at":"2026-08-08"}
research/audit/wave7-dispatch/audit-beta-topology-uniform.log-307131-+{"id":"lem-normal-sequences-of-entourages","statement":"ai-altered","proof":"ai-generated","evidence":"established-knowledge","urls":["https://math.berkeley.edu/~wodzicki/H104.F13/UniformStructure-alt.pdf","https://www.mat.univie.ac.at/~mike/teaching/ss16/general_topology.pdf"],"rationale":"ESCALATED TO ALPHA. Iterated symmetric entourage roots are the standard normal-sequence construction in both sources, but the Statement makes the strictly weaker foundational hypothesis DC explicit and no located source states that same choice-calibrated proposition. It is established, not novel; the recursion proof is local.","alpha_concurred":false,"at":"2026-08-08"}
research/audit/wave7-dispatch/audit-beta-topology-uniform.log-307132-+{"id":"lem-pseudometric-from-a-normal-entourage-sequence","statement":"literature-derived","proof":"ai-altered","evidence":"exact-source","urls":["https://math.berkeley.edu/~wodzicki/H104.F13/UniformStructure-alt.pdf","https://www.mat.univie.ac.at/~mike/teaching/ss16/general_topology.pdf"],"rationale":"Both sources state the normal-sequence metrization lemma with the same dyadic control inclusions and path-infimum pseudometric construction. The proof is a notation-adjusted expansion.","alpha_concurred":false,"at":"2026-08-08"}
research/audit/wave7-dispatch/audit-beta-topology-uniform.log-307133-+{"id":"thm-entourage-uniformities-are-generated-by-gauges","statement":"ai-altered","proof":"ai-altered","evidence":"established-knowledge","urls":["https://math.berkeley.edu/~wodzicki/H104.F13/UniformStructure-alt.pdf","https://www.mat.univie.ac.at/~mike/teaching/ss16/general_topology.pdf"],"rationale":"ESCALATED TO ALPHA. The sources prove every uniformity is generated by pseudometrics but assume an ordinary classical background; the item isolates DC as sufficient. The theorem is standard, but no source with the same foundational hypothesis surfaced.","alpha_concurred":false,"at":"2026-08-08"}
research/audit/wave7-dispatch/audit-beta-topology-uniform.log:307134:+{"id":"thm-three-definitions-of-uniform-space-are-equivalent","statement":"ai-altered","proof":"ai-generated","evidence":"established-knowledge","urls":["https://encyclopediaofmath.org/wiki/Uniform_space","https://math.berkeley.edu/~wodzicki/H104.F13/UniformStructure-alt.pdf","https://www.mat.univie.ac.at/~mike/teaching/ss16/general_topology.pdf"],"rationale":"ESCALATED TO ALPHA. Literature gives the entourage-cover equivalence and pseudometric generation, but not this exact compound ZF/DC calibration. This is a standard synthesis, not an invented theorem; the proof composes the preceding results.","alpha_concurred":false,"at":"2026-08-08"}
research/audit/wave7-dispatch/audit-beta-topology-uniform.log-307135-+{"id":"def-cauchy-filter-in-a-uniform-space","statement":"literature-derived","proof":"not-applicable","evidence":"exact-source","urls":["https://math.berkeley.edu/~wodzicki/H104.F13/UniformStructure-alt.pdf","https://encyclopediaofmath.org/wiki/Uniform_space"],"rationale":"The sources use the same requirement that for every entourage a filter member have square contained in it; notation and equivalent cover wording are the only differences.","alpha_concurred":false,"at":"2026-08-08"}
research/audit/wave7-dispatch/audit-beta-topology-uniform.log-307136-+{"id":"lem-convergent-filters-are-cauchy","statement":"literature-derived","proof":"ai-altered","evidence":"exact-source","urls":["https://math.berkeley.edu/~wodzicki/H104.F13/UniformStructure-alt.pdf"],"rationale":"Wodzicki Exercise 41 states exactly that every filter convergent in the uniform topology is Cauchy. The item supplies the standard symmetric-root proof, with a missing direct citation proposed at A3.","alpha_concurred":false,"at":"2026-08-08"}
research/audit/wave7-dispatch/audit-beta-topology-uniform.log-307137-+{"id":"lem-cauchy-filter-with-a-cluster-point-converges","statement":"literature-derived","proof":"ai-altered","evidence":"exact-source","urls":["https://math.berkeley.edu/~wodzicki/H104.F13/UniformStructure-alt.pdf"],"rationale":"Wodzicki Exercise 45 states that every adherence point of a Cauchy filter is its convergence point. The proof expands this and needs the induced-topology citation recorded at A3.","alpha_concurred":false,"at":"2026-08-08"}
research/audit/wave7-dispatch/audit-beta-topology-uniform.log-307138-+{"id":"def-complete-uniform-space","statement":"literature-derived","proof":"not-applicable","evidence":"exact-source","urls":["https://math.berkeley.edu/~wodzicki/H104.F13/UniformStructure-alt.pdf","https://encyclopediaofmath.org/wiki/Complete_uniform_space"],"rationale":"Both sources define completeness as convergence of every Cauchy filter, exactly as the item does.","alpha_concurred":false,"at":"2026-08-08"}
research/audit/wave7-dispatch/audit-beta-topology-uniform.log-307139-+{"id":"def-uniform-embedding-and-uniform-isomorphism","statement":"ai-altered","proof":"not-applicable","evidence":"semantic-source","urls":["https://encyclopediaofmath.org/wiki/Uniform_space","https://math.berkeley.edu/~wodzicki/H104.F13/UniformStructure-alt.pdf"],"rationale":"The literature uses the same uniform-isomorphism and subspace-uniformity notions. The item packages the embedding and isomorphism definitions in library notation.","alpha_concurred":false,"at":"2026-08-08"}
research/audit/wave7-dispatch/audit-beta-topology-uniform.log-307140-+{"id":"def-completion-of-a-uniform-space","statement":"ai-altered","proof":"not-applicable","evidence":"semantic-source","urls":["https://encyclopediaofmath.org/wiki/Uniform_space","https://math.berkeley.edu/~wodzicki/H104.F13/UniformStructure-alt.pdf","https://encyclopediaofmath.org/wiki/Complete_uniform_space"],"rationale":"The sources define completion by a complete separated target with dense canonical image and induced original uniformity. The item explicitly permits a noninjective Hausdorff reflection map, the equivalent convention for nonseparated inputs.","alpha_concurred":false,"at":"2026-08-08"}
